{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The rider is not carrying the disputed charge. The fare breakdown records the 6.50 SGD as already refunded to the rider and recovered from the driver (payment_status REFUNDED, refund_issued_sgd 6.50), and the trip record shows the same reversal at 17:00:40 ('refunded to rider and withheld from driver pending review'). POL-GEN-03 defines NO_ACTION as the filing party's claim not being supported and the present state standing, and says in terms that NO_ACTION 'never means restore a charge'. The driver's filing asks for exactly that restoration - his compensation back - and this trip's record supplies him no positive entitlement that the interim reversal displaced, so the present state must stand.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-05060", "EV-TRIP-05060"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.payment_status",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver asks for the whole 6.50 SGD back as 'my compensation', but that sum is not the fee this policy fixes. POL-NS-22 transfers to the driver, as compensation for time and fuel, a no-show cancellation fee of 5.00 SGD, and POL-NS-26 fixes the no-show fee at 5.00 SGD. The fare breakdown's own money block reports fee_matches_policy false, with policy_fee_sgd 5.00 against fee_charged_sgd 6.50, and the rider's own statement objects to precisely that excess ('more than the $5 I know about'). The 1.50 SGD above the policy fee is an amount the policy does not authorise as a fee at all, so it cannot be compensation for the driver's time and fuel and cannot be moved back to him; POL-NS-22's prescribed handling of a charge that is not 5.00 SGD is a referral naming that clause, which records the amount error rather than validating it.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-05060"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-22", "POL-NS-26"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.derived.money.fee_matches_policy",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "If the Judge is not satisfied that this record establishes the rider's non-appearance, the case belongs with a human. The only trace in the case is the driver's own device trace: its rider track is empty and it carries no rider-side data at all, so on the fact a no-show charge presupposes - that the rider was not at the pickup - the record offers only the driver's side. POL-GEN-26 provides that where a fact a rule of this version needs cannot be established on the evidence, the case is escalated and the open question stated, with no outcome inferred from the absence; and an escalated fee is held rather than collected, so the rider's refund should not be disturbed while that question is answered.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-05060", "EV-TRIP-05060"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-26"],
      "relies_on": "gps_trace.payload.rider_track",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "DRIVER_COMPENSATION",
    "amount_sgd": 6.5,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": 6.5,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-NS-22: refer the fee-amount discrepancy — the record charged 6.50 SGD where POL-NS-22 fixes the no-show fee at 5.00 SGD — for review; the money ruling acts on the amount actually charged."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "Outcome: the no-show fee stands, and the 6.50 SGD refunded to the rider and recovered from the driver is to be paid back to the driver, so the driver receives 6.50 SGD (DRIVER_COMPENSATION; amount_sgd and driver_compensation_sgd carry the same figure, 6.50).\n\nTo the driver: every no-show condition is on the record. The trip was on-demand with no scheduled time, so under POL-NS-21 the 300-second free wait ran from your arrival at 14:09:15 and expired at 14:14:15; you cancelled at 14:15:40, after it. Your arrival is corroborated on the category's arrival test — the nearest GPS fix (14:09:55) is 2.89 m from the recorded pickup, inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius and inside the 25 m accuracy filter, with 4 m accuracy reported. Under POL-NS-23 you sent two in-app messages (14:09:40 and 14:13:00) and placed an in-app call (14:12:10), all before the 14:15:40 cancellation, so the contact obligation is met and no FULL_REFUND arises under that clause. The trace also shows you stationary at the pickup from 14:09:25 to 14:15:25, so POL-NS-24 (driver no-show) is not triggered — you did arrive — and no 5.00 SGD goodwill credit is due.\n\nTo the rider: your objection is the amount — you were charged 6.50 SGD, not the 5.00 SGD the policy fixes — and that is correct on the record: the fare breakdown reports fee_matches_policy false, with policy_fee_sgd 5.00 against fee_charged_sgd 6.50. But POL-NS-22's own answer to a charge other than 5.00 SGD is to rule on the amount charged and add a referral; it does not void the fee, and POL-NS-26 fixes the fee without making an amount error a ground for refunding it. The referral above sends the 6.50-versus-5.00 discrepancy for review. The no-show itself is not denied on this record: the platform's wait timer expired with the rider not on board, the driver's call went unanswered, and your own statement accepts the charge was a no-show charge.\n\nOn the escalation argument under POL-GEN-26: no rule here needs a rider-side trace. The facts the no-show rules require — arrival, the free wait, contact before cancelling, and the fee charged — are carried by COMPLETE artifacts at weight 1.0 (trip record EV-TRIP-05060, GPS trace EV-GPS-05060, chat log EV-CHAT-05060, fare breakdown EV-FARE-05060). The only absent artifact, the traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-05060-01 (MISSING, weight 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT), carries no fact and is not required by any no-show rule, so its absence leaves no open question and no ground to hold the fee.\n\nThe deciding facts rest on artifacts at weight 1.0, so the confidence cap is 1.0. The dispute value is 6.50 SGD, below POL-GEN-22's 10.00 SGD band, and neither profile carries a fraud flag (both fraud_flags 0), so no minimum confidence applies (POL-GEN-22, POL-NS-26); no safety indicator is present (POL-GEN-21). No referral arises under POL-NS-24 (no goodwill credit) or POL-NS-25 (the repeat no-show counter is not present on the rider profile)."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "DRIVER_COMPENSATION",
    "amount_sgd": 6.5,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": 6.5,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-NS-22: the record charged 6.50 SGD, not the 5.00 SGD policy fee (EV-FARE-05060, fee_matches_policy false); the ruling acts on the amount charged and refers the 1.50 SGD discrepancy for review."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "Driver D-62878, your claim succeeds. Rider R-81472, the 6.50 SGD refunded to you on 29 Aug 2026 is paid over to the driver, because the no-show charge on trip TRP-05060 was validly earned.\n\nThe fee stands. TRP-05060 was an on-demand booking with no scheduled pick-up time, so under POL-NS-21 the 300-second (5-minute) free wait ran from the driver's arrival at 14:09:15 (trip record EV-TRIP-05060). The driver's device trace EV-GPS-05060 (25 fixes, 100% coverage, no gap over 120 s, weight 1.0) shows him stationary at the pick-up from 14:09:25, with the nearest fix 2.89 m from the recorded pick-up point - inside the 50 m STANDARD-zone arrival radius and inside the 25 m accuracy filter (accuracy 4 m) - so the arrival is corroborated, not a bare button press. The wait expired at 14:14:15 and the driver cancelled at 14:15:40, 385 s after it began, so POL-NS-21 and the precondition POL-NS-22 sets are satisfied.\n\nThe contact obligation in POL-NS-23 is met. Before cancelling, the driver sent two in-app messages (14:09:40 and 14:13:00, both delivered and read) and placed one in-app call (14:12:10); the chat log EV-CHAT-05060 and the trip record's in-app call entry agree. Neither limb is missing, so no FULL_REFUND arises under that clause, and POL-NS-24 (driver no-show) is not in point because the driver was at the pick-up and ready - it gives you neither a refund nor the 5.00 SGD goodwill credit.\n\nRider, your three arguments do not change this. (1) You say the present state must stand and NO_ACTION is the outcome (EV-FARE-05060, POL-GEN-03). The 29 Aug reversal was expressly interim - 'refunded to rider and withheld from driver pending review' - not a finding that the money was yours. That review is now done and the charge was validly earned. POL-GEN-03's remark that NO_ACTION 'never means restore a charge' concerns a charge the platform wrongly collected; here a valid charge was collected and then held back from the driver, who is entitled to it. (2) You say the 1.50 SGD above the policy fee cannot be the driver's compensation (EV-FARE-05060, POL-NS-22, POL-NS-26). POL-NS-22 prescribes exactly what happens when the record charges more than 5.00 SGD: the ruling acts on the amount charged and a referral is added - the fee-amount check is a referral that never suppresses the money (POL-GEN-03) - and that is what this ruling does. (3) You say the case must go to a human under POL-GEN-26 because the only trace is the driver's device trace with an empty rider track. No fact these rules need is unestablished: the driver's arrival, the free wait and the message-and-call obligation are each carried by complete artifacts at weight 1.0 (EV-TRIP-05060, EV-GPS-05060, EV-CHAT-05060). The only absent artifact is the traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-05060-01 (weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT), and no no-show clause requires traffic data, so its absence leaves no open question. Your own statement - that 6.50 SGD was charged, that it was more than the 5.00 you knew of, and that 'then it was refunded, fine' - accepts the charge was a no-show charge and disputes only the amount, which is the referral point, not a ground to keep the money.\n\nWhat moves. The record charged and refunded 6.50 SGD (EV-FARE-05060: fee_charged_sgd 6.50, refund_issued_sgd 6.50); the policy fee is 5.00 SGD (POL-NS-22, POL-NS-26); the money block reports fee_matches_policy false and driver_compensation_if_upheld_sgd 6.50. The ruling therefore moves 6.50 SGD to driver D-62878: amount_sgd and driver_compensation_sgd are both 6.50 SGD.\n\nReferral. POL-NS-22 requires a referral where the record charged an amount other than the 5.00 SGD policy fee; the 1.50 SGD excess is referred for review.\n\nConfidence. 0.95. The disputed value is 6.50 SGD, below POL-GEN-22's 10.00 SGD band, neither profile carries a fraud flag, and POL-NS-26 makes the AI ruling final on a no-show, so no minimum confidence applies and none is wanting. The facts that decide this case are carried by artifacts whose weights are 1.0, so the cap is 1.0."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
